      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-3.avif" alt="" />
    </div>

    <!-- Column 2 Text -->
    <div slot="col-2-text">
      <p>
        Farming is so healthy and rewarding, <br />
        For as the soil you till; <br />
        You are living close to nature, <br />
        As you perform our Saviour’s will.
      </p>

      <p>
        We’ve been put upon this planet, <br />
        To cultivate the land; <br />
        Sowing, tending, harvesting, <br />
      </p>

      <p>
        He who guides the growing force, <br />
        The sunshine and the rain; <br />
        Filling streams with water, <br />
        And swelling ears of grain.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 3 Middle Images -->
    <div slot="col-3-images">
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-10.avif" alt="" />
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-5.avif" alt="" />
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-12.avif" alt="" />
    </div>

    <!-- Column 4 Text -->
    <div slot="col-4-text">
      <p>
        Ripening fruit and vegetables, <br />
        Grown for us all to eat; <br />
        The grass for sheep and cattle, <br />
        A source of milk and meat.
      </p>

      <p>
        Wool for coats and blankets, <br />
        To keep out the winter chill; <br />
        If we work with our Provider, <br />
        He will all our needs fulfil.
      </p>

      <p>
        Yes! Farming families down the years, <br />
        Have been our Earth’s mainstay; <br />
        So we thank our Lord for the Harvest, <br />
        In our heartfelt prayers today.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 5 Images (15%) -->
    <div slot="col-5-images">
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-13.avif" alt="" />
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-14.avif" alt="" />
      <img src="/poems/2018-october/image-16.avif" alt="" />
    </div>
  </poem-grid>
</div>
